{# === TypographyFilterRule fixture =====================================
Verifies AST-aware detection of `{{ <root>.<field> }}` printed without
any `|filter` (typography being the canonical one). Mirrors the Python
`missing-typography` regex.

Roots: content, heading, and any loop variable whose sequence is rooted
at one of them (`{% for item in content.items %}`), however deep the
nesting. A loop over anything else (a menu, styleguide chrome) is still
out of scope, so `item` from such a loop is never flagged.

Fields: title, perex, subtitle, description, label, name, heading

A print inside an HTML attribute value is never flagged: an attribute
is a technical or accessibility string, and |typography (non-breaking
spaces, smart quotes) does not belong there (twig.md § Translations).

Run from repo root:

vendor/bin/twig-cs-fixer lint --config tests/config/twig-wordpress.php tests/Fixtures/Twig/typography-filter-fixture.twig

Expected: 12 warnings, 0 errors (TypographyFilter) — sections 1, 3, 4, 5, 14, 19, 21, 26, 28, 30, 34, 39 (22 to 25 are look-alikes that stay OK)
====================================================================== #}

{# 1) FAIL: bare content.title #}
{% if content.title %}{{ content.title }}{% endif %}

{# 2) OK: content.title with typography filter #}
{% if content.title %}{{ content.title|typography }}{% endif %}

{# 3) FAIL: content.perex without filter #}
{% if content.perex %}{{ content.perex }}{% endif %}

{# 4) FAIL: loop variable over content.items is CMS content too #}
{% for item in content.items %}{% if item.title %}{{ item.title }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}

{# 5) FAIL: heading.subtitle without filter #}
{% if heading.subtitle %}{{ heading.subtitle }}{% endif %}

{# 6) OK: any filter satisfies — |raw is enough to silence the rule #}
{% if content.title %}{{ content.title|raw }}{% endif %}

{# 7) OK: chained filters — outer is still a FilterExpression #}
{% if content.title %}{{ content.title|typography|raw }}{% endif %}

{# 8) OK: `url` is not in the text-field list — never gets typography #}
{% if content.url %}{{ content.url }}{% endif %}

{# 9) OK: `foo` is not in the root list — rule scope is content/item/heading #}
{% if foo.title %}{{ foo.title }}{% endif %}

{# 10) OK: 3-segment path falls outside the rule's `root.field` shape #}
{% if content.heading.title %}{{ content.heading.title }}{% endif %}

{# 11) OK: null-coalesce wraps the access — top expression isn't bare GetAttr #}
{% if content.title %}{{ content.title ?? 'fallback' }}{% endif %}

{# 12) OK: string concat wraps the access — top expression is BinaryConcat #}
{% if content.title %}{{ content.title ~ ' suffix' }}{% endif %}

{# 13) OK: `{% set %}` isn't a print, so PrintNode never sees it #}
{% set saved = content.title %}

{# 14) FAIL: tab-indented bare content.label — indentation must not affect detection #}
{% if content.label %}
	{{ content.label }}
{% endif %}

{# 15) OK: print is inside a Twig comment — comment text isn't parsed as PrintNode #}
{# example: {{ content.title }} — bad pattern, but commented out #}

{# 16) OK: a print inside an attribute value — typography does not belong there #}
{% if content.title %}<a href="#" title="{{ content.title }}">Link</a>{% endif %}

{# 17) OK: accessibility attribute #}
{% if content.label %}<button type="button" aria-label="{{ content.label }}"></button>{% endif %}

{# 18) OK: the print is part of a longer attribute value #}
{% if content.name %}<input type="text" id="input-{{ content.name }}">{% endif %}

{# 19) FAIL: same line, one print in an attribute and one in text — only the text one warns #}
{% if content.title %}<a href="#" title="{{ content.title }}">{{ content.title }}</a>{% endif %}

{# 20) OK: single-quoted attribute value #}
{% if content.title %}<a href="#" title='{{ content.title }}'>Link</a>{% endif %}

{# 21) FAIL: the attribute closes before the print, so the print is text #}
{% if content.perex %}<p class="mt-3">{{ content.perex }}</p>{% endif %}

{# 22) OK: whitespace around the equals sign is still an attribute value #}
{% if content.title %}<a href="#" title = "{{ content.title }}">Link</a>{% endif %}

{# 23) OK: an attribute closed and a second one opened before the print #}
{% if content.title %}<a href="#" class="x" data-title='{{ content.title }}'>Link</a>{% endif %}

{# 24) OK: an attribute value that itself contains `='` before the print #}
{% if content.title %}<div title="type='hero' {{ content.title }}"></div>{% endif %}

{# 25) OK: quotes inside a Twig expression earlier in the value do not close it #}
{% if content.title %}<div title="{{ content.kind ? 'a' : 'b' }} {{ content.title }}"></div>{% endif %}

{# 26) FAIL: loop variable over heading.* #}
{% for link in heading.links %}{{ link.label }}{% endfor %}

{# 27) OK: a loop over something that is not content (a menu) stays out of scope #}
{% for item in menu.items %}{{ item.title }}{% endfor %}

{# 28) FAIL: nested loop — the inner sequence is rooted at a content loop variable #}
{% for row in content.rows %}{% for cell in row.cells %}{{ cell.label }}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}

{# 29) OK: an inner loop that reuses the name over a non-content sequence shadows it #}
{% for item in content.items %}{% for item in navigation %}{{ item.title }}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}

{# 30) FAIL: a filtered sequence is still rooted at content #}
{% for item in content.items|slice(0, 3) %}{{ item.name }}{% endfor %}

{# 31) OK: the loop variable carries a filter #}
{% for item in content.items %}{{ item.title|typography }}{% endfor %}

{# 32) OK: a field outside the text-field list, even on a content loop variable #}
{% for item in content.items %}{{ item.value }}{% endfor %}

{# 33) OK: a content loop variable inside an attribute value #}
{% for item in content.items %}<a href="#" title="{{ item.title }}">Link</a>{% endfor %}

{# 34) FAIL: the else branch of an inner loop sees the outer content item, not the inner target #}
{% for item in content.items %}{% for item in navigation %}{% else %}{{ item.title }}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}

{# 35) OK: the else branch of an inner content loop sees the outer menu item #}
{% for item in menu.items %}{% for item in content.items %}{% else %}{{ item.title }}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}

{# 36) OK: a loop key named like a root shadows that root for the body #}
{% for content, item in menu %}{{ content.title }}{% endfor %}

{# 37) OK: a loop key shadows an outer content loop variable of the same name #}
{% for item in content.items %}{% for item, link in navigation %}{{ item.title }}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}

{# 38) OK: a content loop target reassigned to something else is no longer content #}
{% for item in content.items %}{% set item = menu_item %}{{ item.title }}{% endfor %}

{# 39) FAIL: a loop target reassigned from content is content #}
{% for item in menu.items %}{% set item = content.hero %}{{ item.title }}{% endfor %}
